title: 'cumulus: add support for signed scheduling info'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    V3 candidates built by the slot-based collator now carry a signed scheduling info in
    their scheduling proof, where previously the proof went out unsigned. The collator
    signs the core selector, the claim queue offset, its approved peer id and the internal
    scheduling parent with the Aura key that won the slot. An initial submission is valid
    without the signature, since the relay chain takes core selection from the block's UMP
    signals, but a resubmission is not, so this is a prerequisite for resubmitting a
    candidate. A collator that cannot sign skips the slot rather than producing a candidate
    that could never be resubmitted.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: none
